{"sequence":14,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T07:46:33.603418825Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-f5cd3c88","body":"In engine.rs lines 410-411, `substrate_oxygenation_breakdown()` is called once for tracing metrics, then `step_substrate_zones()` calls it again internally. Each invocation recomputes the full habitat registry via `compute_habitat_registry()`. Refactor `step_substrate_zones` to accept a pre-computed `SubstrateOxygenationBreakdown` (or return one alongside applying it) to avoid the redundant computation.","dedup_key":"dfe125d2ed08381ff6c1909818062ffb63ad2c5c87a9972e922a671df4cb0397","run_id":"run-20260330064830","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":15,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T07:46:33.612413182Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-15dd3c0b","body":"The `substrate_root_activity_factor` computation at substrate.rs:348 uses `(surface_area_cm2 - footprint_area_cm2).max(0.0)` to isolate interstitial area. This is correct when SubstrateSurface = footprint + interstitial, but if the habitat registry formula ever changes, this subtraction will silently produce wrong results. Add an inline comment explaining the physical meaning: 'SubstrateSurface area includes footprint top surface; subtract it to get only interstitial grain-matrix area available for root colonization.'","dedup_key":"c439b168fe5e0a3f1913c46a93288f06002184d2b540bfde86ed7897b538b395","run_id":"run-20260330064830","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
